{:edb/db-before-t 1289 :edb/db-after-t 1290 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534602 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:08:05.449Z" 13194139534602 true] [17592186082924 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola\n$4 y^2 - 10 x^2 - 8 y - 40 x = 76$?" 13194139534602 false] [17592186082924 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$4 y^2  - 10 x^2 - 8 y  - 40 x  = 76?$" 13194139534602 true] [17592186082924 1145 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4y^{2} - 10x^{2} - 8y - 40x &= 76 \\\\\n4y^{2} - 8y - 10x^{2} - 40x &= 76 \\\\\n4[y^{2} - 2y] - 10[x^{2} + 4x] &= 76 \\\\\n4[(y - 1)^{2} - 1] - 10[(x + 2)^{2} - 4] &= 76 \\\\\n4(y - 1)^{2} - 4 - 10(x + 2)^{2} + 40 &= 76 \\\\\n4(y - 1)^{2} - 10(x + 2)^{2} &= 76 - 40 + 4 \\\\\n4(y - 1)^{2} - 10(x + 2)^{2} &= 40 \\\\\n((y - 1)^{2})/(10) - ((x + 2)^{2})/(4) &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-2,1)$." 13194139534602 false] [17592186082924 1145 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-10{x}^{2}-8y-40x & =76 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-8y-10{x}^{2}-40x & =76 \\\\ 4[{y}^{2}-2y]-10[{x}^{2}+4x] & =76 \\\\ 4[(y-1)^{2}-1]-10[(x+2)^{2}-4] & =76 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-4-10(x+2)^{2}+40 & =76 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-10(x+2)^{2} & =76-40+4 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-10(x+2)^{2} & =40 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-2,1)$." 13194139534602 true] [17592186082991 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} - \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{4} = 1 ?$" 13194139534602 true] [17592186082991 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} - \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{4} = 1$?" 13194139534602 false] [17592186082991 1145 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k = 2$.\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,2)$." 13194139534602 false] [17592186082991 1145 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k = 2.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,2).$" 13194139534602 true] [17592186082992 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(y+3)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} = 1 ?$" 13194139534602 true] [17592186082992 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(y+3)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} = 1$?" 13194139534602 false] [17592186082992 1145 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-(-3))^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k=-3$.\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,-3)$." 13194139534602 false] [17592186082992 1145 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-(-3))^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,-3).$" 13194139534602 true] [17592186082993 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola\n$x^2 - 4 y^2- 2 x + 16 y = 31$?" 13194139534602 false] [17592186082993 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/assets/57e159560b79e8383e6a2eec7